Add a Remote Query producer through the ClickHouse check's standard optional execution interface: execute a validated query exactly once through a dedicated streaming client with read-only server settings and send/receive timeouts derived from the remaining run budget, streaming the bounded server-rendered rows to its-agent-intake as one synchronous request per page using the spec-driven intake protocol. Producer runs also open native ddtrace producer spans at the producer's phase boundaries through the shared base tracing machinery — development-only, gated behind the development tracing switch and an explicitly set `DD_TRACE_AGENT_URL` endpoint, failing closed — and fail-open otherwise. Successful execute answers carry status only after intake finalization; upload identity and totals are not returned to the Agent.
